WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.500
Which card should I use? A $100.00 cart at Sample Kitchen, a fictional store; your cards: Double Cash, Quicksilver, Freedom Unlimited, Blue Cash Everyday.

2
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:12.000
Your best card, right on your cart. The badge: Use Freedom Unlimited · $3.00 back. Its panel: based on $100.00 cart estimated total at Sample Kitchen, treated as a restaurant.

3
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:19.000
The rule, in the issuer’s words: 3% on “dining at restaurants, including takeout and eligible delivery services”. Then Double Cash $2.00, Quicksilver $1.50, Blue Cash Everyday $1.00.

4
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:25.500
Amounts only when certain. A gift card is applied, so the cart amount isn’t read; the badge ranks your cards by rate: Blue Cash Everyday 3%, Double Cash 2%, Quicksilver 1.5%, Freedom Unlimited 1.5%.

5
00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:33.000
Card terms kept current by an LLM; every change approved by a person. No model at checkout. Your cards are saved in your browser. Usage reports only if you choose Share.

6
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:38.000
AI Checkout. The best card you already own, shown right on your cart. Works at any U.S. online store. Illustration with sample cards and a fictional store.
